WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.650
Your friend holds up a pen and says:

2
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:05.210
«Mon stylo est bleu.» You want to answer,

3
00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.960
'Mine is red.' Not 'my pen'.

4
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:12.070
Just 'mine'. Then you spot
two jackets on a chair.

5
00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:14.510
You want this one, not that one.

6
00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:17.120
And you don't want to say 'jacket' twice.

7
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.780
So how do you say 'this one',

8
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.940
'that one' and 'mine' in French
without repeating the noun?

9
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:25.670
In this mission, you'll start with «ça»,

10
00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:29.260
the word French uses to
point at a thing or an idea.

11
00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:32.510
Then you'll explore a whole
grid of words for 'mine',

12
00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:35.450
'yours', 'his', 'hers' and more.

13
00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.210
Your mission: find out how French points,

14
00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:41.400
compares and claims
without repeating a noun.
